  "id": "COMPOUND:138 - PROTEIN:4978",
  "verbalization": "Pyridoxal, a vitamin B6 derivative, is implicated in the target pathway leading to C8166 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Pyridoxal interacts with Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including methyl (1S,4aR,6S,7R,7aR)-6-...-carboxylate and [(2S,3S,4aS,8R,8aS)-3-hydroxy-...-yl] acetate. These compounds are all linked to C8166, indicating a potential pathway where Pyridoxal may influence the activity of these targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Pyridoxal in modulating the biological activity of these compounds, which could be relevant in understanding its function in the context of C8166. The evidence supports a mechanism where Pyridoxal acts as a modulator of the target pathways, potentially influencing the downstream effects of these compounds on C8166.",
